---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE } from '../consts';

const schema = [
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'WebPage',
    name: 'Support',
    url: new URL('/support', SITE.url).href,
    description:
      'How to report a problem with an iHateAudio tool, and how to use the tools from ChatGPT, Claude or another AI assistant.',
    publisher: { '@id': `${SITE.url}/#organization` },
  },
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'BreadcrumbList',
    itemListElement: [
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 1, name: 'All tools', item: SITE.url },
      {
        '@type': 'ListItem',
        position: 2,
        name: 'Support',
        item: new URL('/support', SITE.url).href,
      },
    ],
  },
];
---

<Base
  title="Support: Report a Problem"
  description="Report a problem with an iHateAudio tool, and see how to use the tools from ChatGPT, Claude or another AI assistant through MCP."
  path="/support"
  schema={schema}
>
  <div class="wrap page prose">
    <h1>Support</h1>
    <p class="toolhead__sub" style="margin-bottom: var(--s8)">
      Something broke or did the wrong thing? Email
      <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>What helps us fix it</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Which tool, and whether you used the website or an AI assistant (which one).</li>
      <li>Your browser and device.</li>
      <li>The file type, and roughly how long the file is.</li>
      <li>What you expected, and what happened instead.</li>
      <li>Any error message, word for word.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      You do not need to send the audio. If a problem only happens with one
      file, say so and we will ask for it.
    </p>

    <h2>Using iHateAudio in ChatGPT</h2>
    <p>
      Share an audio or video file in the chat and say what you want done, for
      example "remove the silence and normalize it for Spotify". ChatGPT picks
      the tool, runs it, and gives you a link to the result.
    </p>

    <h2>Using iHateAudio from Claude or another MCP client</h2>
    <p>
      Every tool is also available to any assistant that supports MCP, through
      one server: <code>https://ihateaudio.com/mcp</code>. It needs no account
      and no key.
    </p>
    <ol>
      <li>
        In Claude, open Settings, then Connectors, and add a custom connector
        named iHateAudio with the URL <code>https://ihateaudio.com/mcp</code>.
        Other clients have their own place to add an MCP server by URL.
      </li>
      <li>
        Give the assistant a public HTTPS link to the file, one that downloads
        the file directly (a Dropbox link ending in <code>dl=1</code> works, a
        page that shows a player does not).
      </li>
      <li>
        Say what you want done. The assistant picks the tool, runs it, and gives
        you a link to the result.
      </li>
    </ol>

    <h2>Limits, in every assistant</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Each job takes one file. The two joining tools take up to 12.</li>
      <li>Files can be up to 250 MB.</li>
      <li>
        Result links stop working one hour after they are made, and results are
        deleted after one day, so download them first.
      </li>
      <li>
        The voice recorder is not available to assistants, because it needs
        your microphone. Use it on the website.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      How your files are handled through an assistant is on the
      <a href="/privacy">privacy page</a>. The rules of use are in the
      <a href="/terms">terms of service</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>
